{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Take the Levites in place of every firstborn among the children of Israel.</b> The reason that present-day Levites do not redeem the firstborn born to Israelites from now onward is that the present-day Levites were born to Levite fathers who had already redeemed the firstborn of Israel, and logic does not grant them the power to redeem it more than once. And all the present-day firstborn are not from firstborns already redeemed by Levites in the wilderness, but rather are born of ordinary Israelites who were never redeemed. And the firstborns who were redeemed by Levites in the wilderness are not known, so as to exempt those descended from them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:22.425703023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}